# 9. CONFIRMED SIGNALS VS LIVE PREVIEWS

This distinction is essential.

The application must display two different states.

## Confirmed signal

Calculated from the most recent completed candle.

This is the primary published analytical classification.

## Live preview

Calculated using the currently forming candle.

This may change before candle close.

Display a visible "Provisional" label.

For example:

Confirmed: Bullish  
Live preview: Strong Bullish — Unconfirmed

Do not generate permanent historical signal records from unconfirmed candle states.

Create event records only after the relevant confirmation criteria are satisfied.

Handle revised or corrected exchange candle data explicitly.

